{"title":"1987 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems from the <b>1987 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"USAMO\">USAMO</a>.</b>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a08fb31c4bdb128db1151c89381514b88bf9577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m^2+n)(m + n^2)= (m - n)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"235\" height=\"19\" />, where m and n are non-zero integers.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The feet of the angle bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> form a right-angled triangle. If the right-angle is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> is the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" />, find all possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest set of polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/2751d79d3bbfb34440d68c685fe6ba7414951749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> such that: \n</p>\n<dl><dd>1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a092977b152423d3b8edc9c6d8fb4bed0e70f44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" /> belongs to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.</dd>\n<dd>2. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/5/c05cbeb1cf4b5153e365a9253baefde1c97135e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> belongs to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2fb08aedacb622dfa9854bbba718af231e3d29a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\cdot r(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7055b6b8e7b3a88cb58568fc7f732231d8dabe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x + (1 - x) \\cdot r(x) )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> both belong to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.</dd></dl>\n<p>Show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/5/c05cbeb1cf4b5153e365a9253baefde1c97135e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9703e10f151c26e976f124951c28a2dac5f1884d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> are distinct elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/705a2b12c1d119452c80de72dc0f4a65899628f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(x) \\neq s(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f17e1346c7c9bb4f51a1dc76b4e547a9da487c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c117e8403b3b9cf74d2f63f6627aa17c1995e3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> are given in the plane: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> has diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is concentric and has diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d59987c7c0f2f7a64660a428a4b71a266347da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;k&lt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />); <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/85160260d550bf33be28c0a722237c3bc60e8c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> has center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />. We regard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> as fixed. Now consider all straight line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> which have one endpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, one endpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/85160260d550bf33be28c0a722237c3bc60e8c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, and contain the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. For what ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/596f9480ba95639d014bdf63280c424ba7304788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{XB}{BY}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"37\" height=\"39\" /> will the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> have minimal length?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e047bc14560bc613b17fb1ba735bba221764510a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> is a sequence of 0's and 1's. T is the number of triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec57565678fe2a4e713d421b45f511e3a537bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_i, a_j, a_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54db52274b430e27e179fe50ba07bd756c62c30c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;j&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> which are not equal to (0, 1, 0) or (1, 0, 1). For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3c0e0875b8695a1e1e2bb48d8c5e73c4e5245f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74efea4ce02738f0765b2b9d578ceb427631eadc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e49e4f75f0ae44fe7e6a0aef69211da14d9f872a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&lt;i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/1645d206c02ab33bad7aa9263e9f74565fb56bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j = a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> plus the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/248ee41acf29d8dac6d244350970db2cb67e3e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j&gt;i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/173cd3fdd338d6b92a0345a0fcd03ec9ec36f405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j\\neq a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a0f058c03926379f034c1605752dea00c0d908a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T=\\sum_{i=1}^n f(i)\\cdot\\left(\\frac{f(i)-1}2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"199\" height=\"48\" />. If n is odd, what is the smallest value of T?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO\" title=\"1987 USAMO\">1987 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1987\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO\" title=\"1986 USAMO\">1986 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO\" title=\"1988 USAMO\">1988 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043242\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 297/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1209/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 60/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8604/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.648      1 -total\n 56.05%    6.529      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 41.37%    4.819      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9822:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018043242 and revision id 284873. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}